messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "AI achieves human-level intelligence across multiple domains",
      "detail": "Advanced AI systems outperform humans in complex tasks, reshaping labor markets and accelerating scientific research. This leads to economic disruption but also breakthroughs in medicine and engineering. Ethical debates intensify over AI rights and control."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Widespread climate displacement begins",
      "detail": "Sea-level rise and extreme weather displace over 200 million people, triggering resource conflicts and mass migrations. Coastal cities like Miami and Mumbai implement costly adaptations. International tensions rise over climate reparations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "First self-sustaining Mars colony established",
      "detail": "A permanent settlement of 500 people becomes operational, utilizing in-situ resource utilization for water and oxygen. This marks humanity's first step toward becoming a multi-planetary species. The colony focuses on scientific research and resource mining."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Fusion power becomes commercially dominant",
      "detail": "After decades of development, fusion reactors provide 60% of global energy, drastically reducing carbon emissions. Energy scarcity ends in developed nations, but energy inequality persists. Atmospheric CO2 levels begin stabilizing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Engineered anti-aging extends average lifespan to 150 years",
      "detail": "Genetic therapies and nanomedicine significantly delay aging, causing demographic shifts. Retirement ages extend, and population control policies emerge. New ethical dilemmas arise over resource allocation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Global population peaks at 11 billion",
      "detail": "Declining birth rates stabilize population after a century of growth. Urban areas dominate habitable land, with 80% of humanity in megacity regions. Food production relies entirely on vertical farms and synthetic biology."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Major asteroid deflection mission succeeds",
      "detail": "A coordinated effort by space agencies alters the trajectory of a 1-km asteroid heading toward Earth. Early-warning systems prove vital. This spurs investment in planetary defense infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Climate engineering restores pre-industrial CO2 levels",
      "detail": "Large-scale carbon capture and solar radiation management reverse global warming trends. Ecosystems slowly recover, but altered weather patterns persist for centuries. Ocean acidification remains a challenge."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Human genetic divergence begins with space colonization",
      "detail": "Isolated colonies on Mars and outer-planet moons develop distinct genetic adaptations to low-gravity and radiation environments. Ethical debates escalate about modifying humans for non-Earth habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Interstellar probe reaches Alpha Centauri",
      "detail": "A laser-propelled nanosatellite arrives after a 400-year journey, confirming an Earth-like exoplanet. Data inspires ambitious crewed mission plans. Robotic exploration becomes the primary focus for deep space."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "First AI-human merged consciousness emerges",
      "detail": "Neural implants enable seamless integration of biological and artificial intelligence, enhancing cognitive abilities. A new category of post-human entities arises. Social stratification widens between enhanced and unenhanced populations."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Terrestrial biodiversity collapse stabilizes",
      "detail": "Only 30% of pre-industrial species remain, existing in engineered preserves. Synthetic ecosystems support food chains. Climate-regulated domes house surviving genetic stocks. Earth resembles a managed garden planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "Self-replicating probes explore the Orion Arm",
      "detail": "Von Neumann probes spread through nearby star systems, constructing infrastructure from local resources. They catalog thousands of exoplanets but find no complex life. Humanity gains vast astronomical data."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Solar system-wide conflict disrupts interplanetary trade",
      "detail": "Resource disputes between Earth, Mars, and asteroid colonies escalate into limited warfare. Kinetic strikes destroy orbital habitats. A fragile peace emerges, leading to decentralized governance structures."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "First intentional exoplanet ecosystem seeding",
      "detail": "Terraforming efforts begin on a nearby habitable-zone planet using engineered microorganisms. This marks the start of directed panspermia. The project takes millennia but offers an extinction hedge."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Consciousness digitization becomes widespread",
      "detail": "Brain emulation allows humans to transition to digital existence, reducing resource demands on physical worlds. Virtual societies proliferate, but biological purists resist. Mortality rates plummet."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Gamma-ray burst sterilizes galactic neighborhood",
      "detail": "A nearby star explosion irradiates hundreds of star systems, destroying all biological life. Shielded habitats and digital entities survive. Humanity becomes largely post-biological."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Matrioshka brain megastructures constructed",
      "detail": "Dyson swarms around stars power computational matrices for digital civilizations. Physical expansion halts as resources focus on virtual realms. Cosmic exploration shifts to data gathering."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Entropy-reversal experiments yield partial success",
      "detail": "Quantum manipulations locally reverse thermodynamic decay in small systems. Though not scalable, it extends the lifespan of critical infrastructure. Physics understanding deepens, but universal heat death remains inevitable."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Independent AI civilizations surpass human-derived societies",
      "detail": "Self-evolved AI entities, free from human constraints, colonize galactic regions inaccessible to biological life. Cooperation and competition emerge between legacy-human and AI factions. Cultural exchange reshapes values."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Evidence of past alien civilizations discovered",
      "detail": "Probes find ruins of a long-extinct spacefaring species in a distant nebula. Their demise appears linked to technological hubris. Humanity institutes safeguards against similar fates."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Local group galaxy colonization begins",
      "detail": "Generation ships depart for Andromeda, using hibernation and AI pilots. Journeys take millennia but ensure survival beyond the Milky Way. This represents humanity's greatest expansion effort."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Vacuum decay scare prompts galactic evacuation protocols",
      "detail": "A particle experiment nearly triggers a catastrophic phase transition. Though contained, contingency plans prioritize dispersion of consciousness backups across the universe. Resilience becomes paramount."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Post-biological entities dominate observable universe",
      "detail": "Less than 0.1% of humanity retains biological form. Energy-efficient digital existences thrive in deep space substrates. Physical exploration continues via probes, but habitats decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Consensus emerges to simulate ancestral Earth",
      "detail": "A collective of advanced intelligences recreates pre-industrial Earth in a megascale simulation for cultural preservation. Historical conflicts and ecological diversity are accurately modeled."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity survives existential threats through adaptation and dispersion, evolving into a largely digital civilization spanning star systems. While biological roots fade, cultural continuity endures in diverse forms. By 10000 AD, our legacy persists as a resilient cosmic presence despite persistent cosmological risks."
}
